comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:09:25.972Z","harness:codex","Estimate basis 2026-08-03: 900 minutes reflects a cross-call budget ledger, served-fact references, deterministic degradation, session and fleet composition, CI ratchet, and small-workspace no-regression proof."
  "2026-08-03T11:15:45.320Z","harness:codex","Sequencing 2026-08-03: establish trustworthy per-command ceilings in pm-5t33or before composing a session ledger, then use the same receipt and degradation algebra for within-session deduplication. This item implements the agent-facing simplification outcome because fewer commands are insufficient if the prescribed multi-call orientation still repeats a third of its bytes."
  "2026-08-07T05:54:35.716Z","harness:codex","Duplicate/orientation evidence 2026-08-07: searched all 2,343 items across every status for output session token budget, seen/suppression, repeated item context, and closed session-budget predecessors; pm-hid9g1 is the canonical owner. pm-5t33or supplies the shipped per-call budget algebra, pm-sb0tns owns the remaining universal row/projection prerequisite, pm-tch9cs remains the distinct cross-agent amortization horizon."
  "2026-08-07T06:28:08.159Z","harness:codex","Implementation checkpoint 2026-08-07: caller-carried versioned outputSession is now shared by CLI, SDK, MCP schemas, completions, and embedded output. Successive reads carry cumulative spend and a served-item set; repeated item facts become resolvable session:<session-id>:<item-id> references. The same generic row traversal covers nested arrays and object maps. Synthetic orientation calibration now runs context/list/search/get/next at 2 and 2,243 items: spend 3,663/20,000 and 9,999/20,000 tokens, suppressing 3 and 7 repeats. Non-session reads remain on the byte-compatible early-return path, so small trackers pay no default session overhead."
  "2026-08-07T06:53:13.333Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: pnpm test:coverage passed 438 test files and 6,898 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage (49,315 statements, 35,764 branches, 10,074 functions, 47,780 lines; zero uncovered counts). Focused session/parser/object-map/adversarial fixed-point/calibration negative-control tests cover the new contracts without exclusions."
  "2026-08-07T06:58:36.203Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance 2026-08-07: in isolated tracker /tmp/tmp.FoOKATDTEM, built CLI initialized storage and created two real items. First list charged 473/4,000 tokens and carried two seen IDs; second search charged cumulative 879 tokens and replaced both repeated facts with session references. A create invocation carrying --output-session failed closed with exit 2 and item count remained exactly 2."
  "2026-08-07T07:02:21.647Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: strict caller-carried output sessions compose context/list/search/get/next under one 20,000-token ceiling, replace repeated facts with resolvable references, fail closed at exhaustion and on mutation scope, and preserve byte-compatible no-session reads. The CI calibration now permits session bytes/spend only to shrink and suppression only to hold or improve at 2 and 2,243 items. Exact coverage, all quality gates, linked tests, and manual acceptance pass."
  "2026-08-07T07:16:29.199Z","harness:codex","Exact-head static-gate correction after rebasing main: CodeFactor parity measured parseReadOutputSession at 17 against the mandatory 16 ceiling. Replaced sequential field branches with a declarative validation table, preserving strict errors and 100% focused branch coverage while reducing complexity below the gate. No contract or behavior changed."
  "2026-08-07T07:29:41.128Z","harness:codex","Final rebased-head evidence: current origin/main plus this tranche passed 441 test files / 6,917 tests with exact 100% statements (49,640), branches (36,069), functions (10,152), and lines (48,085). ESLint, zero clones, 100% source/export/member docstrings, CodeFactor complexity <=16, SDK/package parity, contracts, 77 token surfaces, secrets, docs, calibration, tracker ratchet, SDK import costs, CLI transport floor, and changelog check all passed. The import-cost subprocess had one load-sensitive miss under concurrent host work, then its isolated mandatory rerun passed without weakening budgets."
  "2026-08-07T07:30:50.067Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/927 reviews the exact-head context-session budgeting, universal transport/schema integration, strict calibration, and generated contract changes. Initial reviewed implementation commit: 48f89b5bba8a663238f1ed66f8902b4da719f1e8."
  "2026-08-07T07:44:26.466Z","harness:codex","Review evidence (PR #927, DeepScan): replaced assertion-mediated session-presence narrowing in scripts/release/context-intent-calibration-gate.mjs with an explicit symmetric undefined guard before property access; added both one-sided-missing negative controls in tests/unit/scripts/release/context-intent-calibration-gate.spec.ts. Focused 10-test suite, ESLint, full TypeScript typecheck, and the real 2/2243-item calibration gate pass. This is follow-up evidence on the closed item; it remains closed and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-07T07:49:44.821Z","harness:codex","Exact review-fix coverage: full pnpm test:coverage passes at 100% statements 49,641/49,641, branches 36,071/36,071, functions 10,152/10,152, and lines 48,086/48,086. The DeepScan guard correction therefore preserves the tranche's mandatory 100/100/100/100 gate."
  "2026-08-07T08:01:04.424Z","harness:codex","GitHub exact-head review loop for c5e95b159: all required Actions and external gates are green, including 4 coverage shards plus aggregator, static, smokes, compatibility, typecheck, Windows, macOS/Linux runtime, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, benchmarks, CodeFactor, Codecov, Hound, and DeepScan (0 new issues). Every bot conversation comment was dispositioned and reacted to. CodeRabbit and Sourcery remained provider-rate-limited and Greptile produced no review after more than the requested 20-minute maximum; these are explicit external limitations, not approvals or hidden findings."
  "2026-08-07T08:23:29.640Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit P1 remediation: session receipts are now attached before the binding remaining-budget decision, reattached after compaction, and included in omission feasibility. A call whose mandatory receipts cannot fit fails closed instead of returning a falsely budget-compliant envelope. New regressions prove both a fresh 256-token session and a later call with exactly 256 tokens remaining return 254-token complete envelopes with exact spent/charged receipts; a larger terminal receipt is rejected. Focused 22-test suite, ESLint complexity ceiling, typecheck, real 2/2243-item calibration, and full coverage pass at exact 100% (49,648 statements, 36,077 branches, 10,152 functions, 48,093 lines)."
  "2026-08-07T08:47:54.341Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI governance evidence: static gate on 73cf0e15f correctly rejected the six newly filed GitHub lineage items because acceptance criteria and estimates were missing, and rejected three new blocks rows under pm-jkbqt8's active non-growth ceiling. Enriched all six issues with measurable acceptance criteria and estimates; removed two redundant blocks-to-parent rows; retained the GH-920/GH-921 companion edge as related because the live pm-jkbqt8 finding proves blocks is not readiness-safe. Released every temporary claim; pm list-in-progress is zero; tracker-measurement-gate passes without changing thresholds."
  "2026-08-07T09:25:17.394Z","harness:codex","Review verification found and closed canonical pm-ay3l0p: the first linked coverage attempts failed because outer PM_SOURCE_* hints overrode the child runner's isolation. The runner now clears those hints at its fresh sandbox boundary, and pm test records the authoritative coverage command passing 441 files / 6,919 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. Direct and linked evidence are now semantically identical."
  "2026-08-07T09:38:39.958Z","harness:codex","Final review-fix head verification: 441 files and 6,919 tests pass at exact 100% statements 49,665/49,665, branches 36,088/36,088, functions 10,158/10,158, and lines 48,110/48,110. Static quality, package boundaries, SDK/public-surface parity, contracts, token budgets, 2/2,243-item calibration, tracker ratchet, SDK import costs, and CLI transport floors also pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T07:02:19.900Z","harness:codex","Cross-call context accounting stays universal and small-workspace-free when the complete versioned ledger travels with the caller. The host can then reuse the same egress row contract across CLI, SDK, MCP, and packages without a daemon, persistent session index, or command-local cache."
